  "why": "The slate's `letter-sign` moved from the counter's beat to the Curator's, which the path plays before the case is pressed and the `set-block` hangs the slate. At that beat the cell is bare wall, so the re-lettering would write to nothing; the build refuses it, naming the beat and the write that places the sign. Its two zh-cn rows move with it, keyed by the beat that now holds them. It declares no unit."
